---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import PayRaiseCalculator from '@/components/tools/calc/PayRaiseCalculator.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="pay-raise-calculator">
  <PayRaiseCalculator client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How the pay raise calculator works</h2>
    <p>
      A percentage raise gives <code>new = old × (1 + raise %)</code>; a fixed raise is added to the old pay. Hourly pay
      becomes yearly pay at <code>rate × hours a week × 52</code>. The real raise takes out inflation:
      <code>(1 + raise) ÷ (1 + inflation) − 1</code>.
    </p>
    <h2>Worked example</h2>
    <p>
      A 4% raise on 60,000 gives 62,400: 2,400 more a year, 200 a month and 92.31 per paycheck every two weeks. At
      40 hours a week that is 30.00 an hour. With 3% inflation, the real raise is 0.97%.
    </p>
    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <p>
      All figures are before tax. The chart repeats the same raise every year, which real pay rarely does; it shows how
      the gap to inflation grows over time.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
